From: Harbottle & Lewis <litigation@harbottle-lewis.example> (Harbottle & Lewis, solicitors for RAM Media)
To: Mr Douvis <douvis@hellenic-culture-ministry.example> (Ministry of Culture, Organising Committee)
Date: 2006-10-31
Subject: RAM Media Limited - acceptance of repudiatory breach

Further to our two earlier letters of today, our client accepts the repudiatory breaches which have now occurred and terminates the Agreement of 10 May 2006. The breaches are:

(1) failure to make payment of the third instalment due on 15th October according to Cl I.3.b);
(2) unreasonably seeking to reduce the contract price with no legal justification and making it plain that you were only prepared to pay significantly reduced sums, and then only at a date that was unclear;
(3) alleging the existence of an agreement said to have been made with Mr Manley and Mr Ciclitira as justification for a complete departure from the terms of the Agreement; our client denies that any such agreement was reached;
(4) by the final paragraph of your letter of 30th October, making it clear that the Ministry no longer intended to be bound by the Agreement.

Harbottle & Lewis

--
RECONSTRUCTED FROM THE PUBLISHED JUDGMENT. Not an original document.
Source: RAM Media v Ministry of Culture of the Hellenic Republic [2008] EWHC 1835 (QB), paras 13, 155.
Sent at 20:05 London time. Wording is the judge's summary of the four grounds; the two earlier letters of that day and the signatory are not stated.
